<html>
<head>
    <title>World-Space HUD</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="engine:/data/ui/rml.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="app:/data/UI/Shared/atlas.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="app:/data/UI/Shared/theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="app:/data/UI/WorldSpace/world_hud.rcss"/>
</head>
<!--
    The screen-space half of this demo. The kiosk and the nameplates are world-space documents
    in the scene; this overlay is drawn over the game view. WorldMarkers.cs adds a marker per
    target to #markers and moves it every frame with camera.WorldToScreenPoint.
-->
<body>
    <button id="back" class="accent" onclick="BackToMenu"><img sprite="arrow-beige-left"/>Menu</button>

    <div id="hint" class="panel">
        <div class="title">World-Space UI</div>
        <div class="parchment page">
            <div>The kiosk and the nameplates are UI documents drawn into the scene (render mode World Space). Hover and click them like any UI.</div>
            <div class="gap">The gold markers are a screen-space overlay placed from world positions every frame.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="row keys">
            <img class="icon" sprite="glyph-target"/><span>Right-drag: orbit    Wheel: zoom    Esc: menu</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="markers"/>
</body>
</html>
